{"schema": 1, "kind": "resolution", "id": "rev-20261123T013214Z-724be6a9:rev-20261123T012552Z-9afaff99:R-1", "ts": "2026-11-23T01:33:54Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.9.1-dev", "branch": "fix/chunk-plan-order", "build": "349886bcd241+dirty"}, "body": {"finding": {"review_id": "rev-20261123T012552Z-9afaff99", "fid": "R-1"}, "disposition": "fixed", "verified_by": "rev-20261123T013214Z-724be6a9", "at_tree": "367cd0e4878cccb88b656eb0f77a59b9fbcb2537", "rationale": null, "members": [{"id": "M1", "disposition": "fixed", "evidence": "plugin/lib/backlog/upstream.py:163-180. For a -dev version, plugin_build now returns evidence.read_plugin_build(root) through a lazy `from .. import evidence`. Its default root is the new _plugin_root() (parents[2] = plugin/), which plugin_version also uses. read_plugin_build (evidence.py:290-324) requires a tracked VERSION (`ls-files --error-unmatch`), scopes `status --porcelain=v2 -- .` to the plugin directory, and adds +dirty, so it closes both trees the finding named. The new tests cover each case. test_a_plugin_root_inside_an_unrelated_repo_reads_none has VERSION present but untracked, so the old work_tree_commit would have returned the home repo's HEAD and failed it. test_uncommitted_plugin_changes_read_dirty expects `<sha12>+dirty`. test_the_default_root_is_the_running_plugin monkeypatches lib.evidence.read_plugin_build, the same module object upstream imports. The test-status evidence is tree-valid at 367cd0e4878c."}, {"id": "M2", "disposition": "fixed", "evidence": "The delta deletes gitstate.work_tree_commit (plugin/lib/gitstate.py, -10 lines). `grep -rn work_tree_commit plugin tests documentation .prawduct/artifacts .prawduct/changes` matches only the build plan's chunk 05 narrative, which records the deletion. No code reference remains. A repeat search for other plugin-build readers (`branch.oid`, `--short`, `read_plugin_build`, `actor.build` over plugin/) finds only evidence.read_plugin_build feeding actor.build and upstream.plugin_build, plus the display-only banner noted under observations."}]}}

